{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792901717,"nonce":"TMwJZEEKkTVv5a1NLeFjXGYh2Bc=","title":"Gc.finalise misses a dead target when the interpreter leaves its handle on the native stack","message":"TestGcFinalizer (testCallbackFiresAfterGc) flips between PASS and WRONG_ANSWER (`FAILVALUES null != collected`) across rebuilds with no semantic change in between: it passed in every gate up to ct1 and failed deterministically from ct2, where the only compiler change was copy propagation resolving copy chains, and it still failed with that change switched off at runtime.\n\nruntime/src/gc.rs counts a registered target as collected only if no stack word between the caller's frame and the stack base equals its handle. When main starts interpreted, the interpreter's own Rust frames can hold a dead copy of the handle (argument buffers for the `register`/`finalise` calls, temporaries), so whether the scan sees it depends on the interpreter binary's frame layout.\n\nRepro (/tmp/gcf on the NUC):\n\n    class Main {\n      static function main() {\n        var called = false;\n        var held:Null\u003cString\u003e = null;\n        var f = new haxe.GcFinalizer(function(v:String) { called = true; held = v; });\n        f.register({id: 1}, \"collected\");\n        eval.vm.Gc.full_major();\n        eval.vm.Gc.full_major();\n        trace(called); trace(held);   // false, null\n      }\n    }\n\nCalling a stack-hungry recursive function between `register` and `full_major` makes it print true/collected: the residue is overwritten.\n\nA fix has to stop treating dead native stack words as roots for interpreted frames, e.g. scan the interpreter's live registers for interpreted frames instead of its native stack, or clear the call argument buffers after each extern call.\n\nSeparately, `rayzor run --llvm --release --tier 3` on the conformance project for this test crashes (SIGSEGV at 0x0 outside JIT code) after several FAILCHECKs; not investigated.","files":null}]}